  "headline": "Evans Trades Aiyuk, Then Gets Him Back for Pocket Change",
  "publicationDraft": "Evans consolidated Mahomes and two reserve players into Rodgers and Allen. Kuhl acquired Fournette just as Tampa Bay promoted him over Ronald Jones, but flipped him to Stover before his breakout. Aiyuk’s preseason hamstring trouble and reduced role were public knowledge; Kuhl cut him October 13. Evans reclaimed him for $4, cut him, then picked him up again in November. By Week 14, Rodgers and Aiyuk combined for 44.24 in Evans’ victory over Mitch while Allen missed the game with COVID. Rodgers ultimately won MVP, and Evans reached the championship. Kuhl had a fine quarterback in Mahomes, but his handling of the supporting assets left plenty of value on the table. The Aiyuk reunion is separate waiver value, not direct trade production.",
